+````markdown name=docs/runbooks/operator_onepage.md
+```text
+Aegis Operator One‑Page — sequence to harden & deploy FL + webhook + calibrator + secure aggregation + privacy tuning
+
+Prereqs:
+- kubectl context for staging/prod
+- vault CLI authenticated (VAULT_ADDR & VAULT_TOKEN)
+- aws CLI configured if using S3 evidence bucket
+- cosign CLI available and COSIGN_KEY_REF in Vault
+- Docker credentials for ghcr.io or registry
+
+Quick command sequence
+
+1) Build & push admission webhook image
+   docker build -t ghcr.io/<org>/admission-webhook:latest -f ops/webhook/Dockerfile ops/webhook
+   docker push ghcr.io/<org>/admission-webhook:latest
+
+2) Generate CA & server cert, create k8s secret (staging)
+   ./ops/webhook/generate_ca.sh aegis aegis-admission-webhook aegis-webhook-tls
+   # This creates aegis-webhook-tls and aegis-webhook-tls-ca secrets in namespace aegis
+
+3) Deploy webhook (helm or kubectl)
+   # Option A: Helm (uses helm/chart)
+   helm install aegis-admission-webhook helm/admission-webhook -n aegis --create-namespace
+   # Option B: kubectl apply k8s manifests
+   kubectl apply -f ops/webhook/deploy_webhook_prod.yaml
+
+4) Create ValidatingWebhookConfiguration (uses CA bundle in secret)
+   ./ops/webhook/generate_vwc_from_secret.sh aegis aegis-admission-webhook aegis-webhook-tls
+
+5) Provision FL clients (example)
+   # Generates a simple cert/key and stores secrets in k8s & Vault
+   ./ops/fl/client_provision.sh operator@example.com client-001
+
+6) Train & register PyTorch calibrator
+   python3 services/safety/calibrator_pytorch_train.py --in data/calib_labels.csv --out-dir /tmp/calibrator_out
+   # upload model artifact and threshold to Vault
+   ./ops/safety/push_calibrator_to_vault.sh /tmp/calibrator_out secret/data/aegis/calibrator 0.8
+
+7) Deploy calibrator service
+   kubectl create secret generic calibrator-model -n aegis --from-file=/tmp/calibrator_out/calibrator.pt --from-file=/tmp/calibrator_out/vectorizer.joblib
+   kubectl run calibrator --image=python:3.10-slim -n aegis --restart=Always --env="CALIBRATOR_MODEL_DIR=/models" --overrides='
+{"spec":{"containers":[{"name":"calibrator","image":"python:3.10-slim","command":["sh","-c","pip install flask joblib torch scikit-learn && mkdir -p /models && cp /tmp/* /models && python3 /app/services/safety/calibrator_pytorch_service.py"],"volumeMounts":[{"name":"modelvol","mountPath":"/tmp"}]}],"volumes":[{"name":"modelvol","secret":{"secretName":"calibrator-model"}}]}}'
+
+8) Run privacy tuning sweep (CI)
+   # Trigger the workflow .github/workflows/privacy_tuning_full.yml via GitHub Actions (workflow_dispatch)
+
+9) Enable FL server behind oauth2-proxy & TLS (see docs/runbooks/production_hardening_playbook.md)
+   - Store MLFLOW creds & COSIGN_KEY_REF in Vault and mirror into Kubernetes secrets via Vault-Agent or CSI
+   - Deploy Flower with serviceAccount aegis-flower-sa and oauth2-proxy in front
+
+10) Secure aggregation pilot
+   - Deploy ops/secure_agg/pysyft_secure_aggregator.py as a private service (docker build & push ops/secure_agg/Dockerfile)
+   - Run ops/secure_agg/pysecure_test.py to verify functionality on small model
+   - If OK, schedule integration sprint to migrate to PySyft/CrypTen (see ops/secure_agg/INTEGRATION_NEXT_STEPS.md)
+
+Notes:
+- For production, ensure all secrets are in Vault and only mirrored into k8s via Vault Agent or CSI driver; do not store raw keys in k8s manifest.
+- Use cosign + Rekor for all image & artifact signing; ensure cosign key reference is available to automation agents (via KMS).
+- Run rotation drills for KMS/HSM and record manifests to evidence bucket.
+
